let __v_250 = Value::from("The height is set at the stem: undo the two bolts on the side and add or remove the spacers under it, which moves the bars 5 to 10mm at a time - tighten them back to just snug and check the steering turns freely. Too far away is a shorter stem, 10 or 20mm shorter, or a bar with less reach; too low for good is more spacers, and if the steerer has none left, a riser bar or a stem with a steeper angle does the same job. Numb or tingling hands is the bars too far or too low, or the saddle tipped nose-down, and it is worth fixing before a long ride rather than riding through.");
